// libpqxx 7 (the C++ client for Postgres), as the courses use it, over the runtime's shared Postgres
// (PGlite, one session): connection, the transaction types (work, transaction<…>, read_transaction,
// nontransaction), exec / exec_params / exec_prepared and their row-count variants, query<T…>,
// query_value, result / row / field with as<T>(), params, prepared statements, quoting, and the
// exception hierarchy (sql_error with its SQLSTATE: unique_violation, check_violation, …).
//
// A transaction holds the single connection from its BEGIN to its COMMIT/ROLLBACK, as a checked-out
// connection would: statements from other threads (and the harness's) wait for it. A transaction
// destroyed without commit() rolls back. The connection string is ignored: every connection reaches
// the same database. Templates live here; the rest is in cppruntime/src/pqxx.cpp.
